{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 1d3ab89425ef967448148584b74e6b951f4329a1, over all four artifacts (internal/gitstore 8bfdf6df, internal/kernel 4b350ba3, internal/app 9acce7fe, internal/service 0c677125). Independent re-review of the repair to the sole blocker in ratified finding d43fb4f7.\n\nREPAIR: The blocker is genuinely repaired, and the atomic-publication assertion is strengthened rather than weakened. Head 1d3ab894 is a single commit on top of the round-1 reviewed head a5ccd18b, and both share merge-base 316d5aeb, which is current main, so the round-1 review carries forward and the delta is exactly three files. The gate is test-only: the one non-nil caller in the whole tree is the service test. Every advance call site remains nil-guarded, and inside advance the gate is nil-checked so Snapshot is not even evaluated in production; a nil gate cannot block, leak, or reorder anything. SetTestGate is called on the fresh per-flight AuditProgress inside snapshotFlight under flightMu, before the goroutine that runs the audit, so goroutine start supplies the happens-before, and each flight owns its own tracker. Both assertions are now deterministic: advance is called with index+1, once per fully verified commit, so the gate fires exactly at Verified 2 against a 30-record chain and 0 \u003c Verified \u003c Total/2 holds by construction rather than by timing. The former 100ms window is now a lower bound on an indefinite hold, and the test additionally asserts that Verified and Total stay frozen across it. Final publication is still proved by DeepEqual against an independent verified fold, plus the quiet-status equality.\n\nFLAKE PROOF at this head: TestProfileMismatchRebuildIsSingleFlightAndPublishesAtomically ran 15/15 green with -race (129.068s) and 15/15 green without -race (85.557s). The non-race run is the more hostile condition for the original failure, because the unslowed verifier is what used to finish inside the window.\n\nARCHITECTURE: Ordinary Git storage (internal/gitstore) is byte-identical between a5ccd18b and this head, so its contract is untouched. Kernel (internal/kernel) gains 11 lines on AuditProgress, which the type documents as reporting-only: nothing in the kernel reads it back and no verification decision depends on it, so the kernel contract is preserved. Application host (internal/app) gains a nil-by-default setter, and production snapshot semantics are unchanged when nil. Composition and transport (internal/service) changes test code only. No layer contract changed, so docs/reference/architecture.md needs no update in this head.\n\nSECURITY: No security delta. The verification semantics reviewed in round 1 (raw object identity and bounds in readObject, SignedContent and SSHSIG parsing, payload ceilings, key rotation, actor and payload binding) live in internal/gitstore, which is byte-identical between the two heads, so the ratified round-1 clean finding carries over unchanged. The new gate is not reachable from untrusted input: it is set only by an in-process Go caller holding the Workspace, never from HTTP, CLI, or log content, and it is nil on every production path. It introduces no race, deadlock, or production pause. I confirmed the hostile suite still reaches the batch verification path at this head with one mutation probe: neutralizing the Ed25519 signature check was killed by internal/gitstore TestVerifySSHSignatureRejectsChangedInputs/changed_content. The mutation ran in a separate throwaway worktree, was restored, and both worktrees were verified clean.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION: The gate is the smallest honest repair. It replaces a timing assumption with an explicit rendezvous, adds no production branch beyond one nil check per verified commit, and removes the polling loop it displaced. I found nothing further to cut without weakening the conditions of satisfaction. The loadCommit batch and non-batch divergence I flagged as non-blocking in round 1 is unchanged here: all envelope, signature, ceiling, target, and tree-binding checks are shared, and only the empty-tree test and the payload-tree read differ by mechanism. scanAfter unification remains a non-blocking follow-up, not needed for correctness of this head.\n\nGATES at the exact head in a clean detached worktree: go build ./... clean; go vet ./... clean; go test ./... -count=1 green across all 25 packages; BenchmarkColdAuditAtDepth50000 at -benchtime=1x completed 50,000 events in 28.67s with 3 git processes (0.0000600 per record), inside the five-minute target. Not merged.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8bfdf6df81393a350612b6125ae367a19bdf645c","head":"1d3ab89425ef967448148584b74e6b951f4329a1","verdict":"approved"}}